vLLM #63350 (https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/63350), backported to v0.32.0.

The scheduler.py part of these commits on vLLM v0.32.0 (5df63a720):

  0c08194ed [Core] Priority scheduling: preempt for a waiting request under KV pressure (cherry-picked from 569183d93)
    Backported to v0.32.0: the make-room call follows 0.32.0's long prefill
    threshold, as v0.32.0 has no local prefill cadence, and
    tests/v1/core/utils.py keeps v0.32.0's create_scheduler signature.
  145ba6331 [Core] Priority scheduling: give up on room before counting growth (cherry-picked from 44937b87a)
  062a47231 [Core] Priority scheduling: count the decodes' growth once without deferred frees (cherry-picked from 0b02a8964)
  dd79faa77 [Core] Priority scheduling: release nothing without victims or deferred frees (cherry-picked from 705e18140)
  35033bf22 [Core] Priority scheduling: skip the prefix lookup when nothing can be preempted (cherry-picked from df5e162f0)
  6ea23d221 [Core] Priority scheduling: take the first waiting request without iterating (cherry-picked from 63e9db63e)
  7d1db90ca [Core] Priority scheduling: check a fit against a bound before counting growth (cherry-picked from e87503f22)
  58ca55361 [Core] Priority scheduling: count make-room's preemptions in scheduler stats (cherry-picked from e2a6975d7)
    Backport: v0.32.0's SchedulerStats and Prometheus logger have no field
    for them, so the scheduler counts the preemptions and make_stats leaves
    them.

